# physics_interp_video_diffusion

Probing whether **CogVideoX-2b internally represents momentum and momentum
conservation**. Videos come from a Kubric/Bullet simulator with exact physics
labels; the model's internal activations are recovered along an inverted latent
trajectory; linear probes are fit from activations to labels.

Method follows `diffusion_interp.pdf` in this directory ("The Invisible Hand of
Physics", Esmati/Nath et al.). Section 3.1 is reverse sampling, Section 4.4 is
the quantitative-variable probing this project extends to momentum.

---

## STATE AS OF HANDOFF (2026-08-16) — §26 CHANGES THE HEADLINE; READ IT FIRST

**The 2026-08-15/16 session** re-examined the momentum results and added a second
physical domain. What changed, in one place:

* **§26 — products are not stored.** The composition test (probe each factor, then
  combine) beats the direct probe on every product/quotient target in the project.
  This revises §3, the project's one positive claim.
* **§26 — oracles are basis-dependent.** "Probe beats oracle" is meaningless
  without naming the basis; mass's excess disappears at a quadratic one.
* **§27 — the pool list was incomplete.** `B.pre`, `A.all`, `B.all` were never in a
  standard run; `velocity_B_pre` was being reported from the *wrong object's* pool.
* **§28 — one open question**, the Δp route to conservation.
* **§23 — the four-velocity concat probe** was run and gains nothing.
* **§24/§25 — a friction domain** was built, redesigned once on request (two balls
  top-down -> one cube, side view), and the flat floor was found visually ambiguous
  between object motion and camera motion. `slide_set_v2` is the fixed set.
* **§29 — a written protocol** for what would actually establish an internal
  momentum variable, with three cheap tests still unrun.
* **§30 — the friction line was run end to end.** mu decodes at 0.93/0.97 from
  leak-free frame-wide pools and sits *at* its kinematic oracle; composition ties
  direct, which **confirms §26's prediction for a linear functional** and sharpens
  the format claim. The mask leak is the worst in the project (`cube_size` is 99%
  pooling mask), and two rows of §25's predicted-null table were wrong.
* **§30a — mu steers, under Joseph et al.'s protocol AND the passive control they
  lack** (obs/passive 2.3, VideoMAE). But re-derivation is *not* established, and
  the test that would show it is 92%-collinear by construction — the fix is
  written down and unrun.
* **§30b — the INLP "sawtooth" is a ridge-alpha artifact.** This revises §18b and
  withdraws a §22 corroboration row.

