## STATE AS OF HANDOFF (2026-08-17b) — §34 IS A POSITIVE, AND WITHDRAWS TWO NEGATIVES

Read §34 before anything about conservation. It changes the project's answer.

* **§34 — Delta-p IS internally represented, and this is the cleanest positive in the
  project.** `momentum_delta` decodes at 0.517 / 0.318 / 0.232 with **p = 0.000
  against 500-permutation grid-max nulls in all three models**, from a
  pre-transformer baseline of ~0 and with a depth curve that rises from zero. §28
  is closed.
* **§34a — the `momentum_conserved` null was an artifact of the target's shape.**
  The classes are concentric in Delta-p space, so a linear map from the **exact**
  Delta-p scores AUC 0.559. The binary label is a *threshold on a norm* — two
  nonlinear steps past what a linear probe can reach. Regress the vector and take
  the norm in the readout: AUC 0.765, **p = 0.006**.
* **§34b — WITHDRAWN: the mass-ratio subspace and INLP results are algebraic.**
  Ridge is linear in Y and `log(m_A/m_B) = log|dv_B| - log|dv_A|`, so
  `w_ratio = w_B - w_A` to 1e-15. The published 16.5/17.7 deg containment was a
  ridge-alpha artifact. Second time an estimator property posed as geometry.
* **§34c — STOP USING THE FIDELITY-MATCHED ORACLE.** Its answer swings from +0.12
  to -0.14 with the analyst's choice of basis. Use the composition test.
* **§34d — use the BOUNDED ratio** `(m_A-m_B)/(m_A+m_B)`, not the log form (vacuous)
  or the raw form (range 0.010-97.8, R2 meaningless).
* **§34f — nonlinear probing does not rescue conservation** (p = 0.060 / 0.200), and
  the *ingredient* is missing: `cos(dv_A, dv_B)` separates the classes at AUC 1.000
  yet decodes at only 0.20-0.24.
* **§34g — the attentive-probe re-capture is DONE** (`outputs_patch_*`, 830 MB +
  6.6 GB, 150/150 each) but **the probe is broken at n=150** — it reads
  `velocity_A_pre` at 0.413 against a linear probe's 0.974. Data is reusable.

**Net effect on the project's story.** Conservation *violations* are detectable
from these representations after all — the earlier negative was a measurement
artifact. Whether the model *applies* the law is still undecided, and §34b shows
the mass-ratio route cannot decide it even in principle.

