## STATE AS OF HANDOFF (2026-08-13) — PART 1 LARGELY ANSWERED, PART 2 WIDE OPEN

This project has **two** questions, and they are in very different states. Keep
them apart when reading anything below.

1. **How, and whether, models internally represent physical properties in
   multi-object video.** Largely answered — one real positive (momentum beats its
   oracle, §3), one clear multi-object result (object addressability, §16), and a
   sharp structural limit on what probing can ever establish (§12).
2. **Whether those properties can be controllably steered — in video *encoders*.**
   Diffusion steering was tried and failed (§5). **No encoder has ever been
   steered here.** This is the open question and where the remaining work is.

**Nothing is blocking and nothing is running.** Read "Experiments run and what
they found" before designing anything new — nearly every obvious next step has
been tried, and the ones that failed mostly failed for *structural* reasons that
no amount of engineering fixes.

